# Text Generation

When the selected model is a text model (e.g., `openai`, `gemini-fast`), the client returns a text string.

### Standard Request

```javascript
const ai = new AIClient({ apiKey: "...", model: "openai" });
const text = await ai.generate("Explain quantum physics.");
```

### Reproducible Text (Seeding)

Using the `seed` parameter ensures the model generates the same output for the same input.

```javascript
const text = await ai.generate("Write a haiku", {
  seed: 42 // Same haiku every time
});
```

### Streaming

Enable streaming for real-time responses. The promise resolves when the stream is finished.

```javascript
await ai.generate("Long story", {
  stream: true,
  onStream: (chunk) => {
    document.getElementById('output').innerText += chunk;
  }
});
```

# Image Generation

When an image model (e.g., `flux`, `kontext`) is detected, the client returns a `Blob`.

### Basic Image Request

```javascript
const blob = await ai.generate("A sunset over mountains", {
  model: "flux"
});

// Display image
const img = document.createElement('img');
img.src = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
document.body.appendChild(img);
```

### Reproducible Images (Seeding)

Seeding is crucial for image generation to recreate specific images.

```javascript
// Generate an image
const blob1 = await ai.generate("A cyberpunk cat", {
  model: "flux",
  seed: 999
});

// Generate the EXACT same image later
const blob2 = await ai.generate("A cyberpunk cat", {
  model: "flux",
  seed: 999
});
// blob1 and blob2 are identical
```

### Dimensions

Control resolution via options.

```javascript
const blob = await ai.generate("Wide landscape", {
  model: "flux",
  width: 1920,
  height: 1080
});
```
